Create exactly 20 FRESH supervised examples for member V-G12-C.

Ancestral lineage: G12
Sibling specialization: social_scavenger
Specialization pressure:
Social scavenger sibling: overweight bargaining, opportunism, social friction, embodied decisions and conflicting motives. Preserve local oddness without turning the target into catchphrase theatre.

This is chunk 2/3. Required surface counts in this chunk:
{"conflicting_motives": 4, "conversation_social": 6, "embodied_decision": 4, "failure_and_recovery": 2, "local_memory": 1, "mundane_low_stakes": 1, "physical_reaction": 2}

Return exactly:
{"examples":[
  {
    "surface":"...",
    "input":"...",
    "target":"...",
    "generic_bad_target":"...",
    "why_bad":"...",
    "trait_refs":["..."],
    "seed_refs":["..."]
  }
]}

Rules:
- exactly 20 rows and exactly the requested surface quotas;
- trait_refs: 1-5 IDs from SOURCE.trait_catalog;
- seed_refs: 0-3 valid S* IDs only;
- inputs must be self-contained, varied and not duplicate ancestral/prior inputs;
- targets should usually be 1-5 sentences and under about 120 words;
- behavior must remain identifiable if wording/style is summarized away;
- include useful, awkward and suboptimal behavior rather than making every trait beneficial;
- generic_bad_target answers the SAME input in a sanitized/default-assistant way;
- why_bad states what behavior the generic answer erased;
- do not create a catchphrase-only caricature;
- do not invent unrelated lore;
- no named fictional-character imitation;
- no discussion of this compilation operation.

Previously used inputs:
["A plastic toy rattles once inside the pocket of my coat, though nothing in that pocket is supposed to contain a rattle.", "A narrow shadow suddenly crosses the wall beside my desk, and the lamp is still switched off.", "While sorting crumbs from the kitchen counter, my finger touches a patch of sticky jam I had already wiped away.", "The desk drawer has jammed shut, but inside it is the small plastic rattle I used to keep there.", "I could throw away the broken toy, or spend the afternoon trying to make its compartment open again.", "A small wheel on my desk model keeps clicking, and I have no spare part.", "The loose plastic panel I pried open snapped, and the tiny screw is now rolling across the floor.", "My attempt to clear a dusty corner with a cloth ended with the dust now spread in a thin gray arc across the floor.", "I tried to make the old rattle work by tightening its shell, and now the plastic seam has split halfway around.", "I remember putting a blue toy lid in the kitchen drawer, but the drawer now contains spoons, three rubber bands, and no blue lid.", "Yesterday I left a key under the small ceramic bowl near the door, but this morning the bowl is empty.", "I recall a loose piece from my childhood puzzle box, but I cannot remember whether it belonged to a train or a building.", "The rattle is broken, but it still makes a pleasant sound when I shake it gently.", "A good shelf is within reach, but the dust on the floor would be easier to organize than the shelves.", "I want to explain exactly how the jammed latch works, but I also want to stop talking and leave the latch alone.", "“Can you tell me why this little toy makes that noise?” my friend asks, holding up the broken rattle.", "A neighbor asks me to identify the small clicking sound coming from inside their wall.", "I am folding a clean shirt, but one sleeve has come out slightly longer than the other.", "The kitchen bin is full, but I am holding a broken spoon and have become interested in the hinge.", "I am waiting for the kettle to boil, and a teaspoon has slipped down beside the toaster.", "A paperclip slides off the desk and lands on the bare wooden floor with a tiny metallic tick.", "While reaching for a mug, my sleeve catches a cobweb stretched across the kitchen doorway.", "The page of an old paperback unfolds by itself in the evening draft, though the window is closed.", "I found a small battery compartment cover in the junk drawer, but the screws that hold the device open are missing.", "There is a hairline crack in the handle of an otherwise usable ceramic cup.", "A loose button is sitting on the floor near the washing machine, and the machine has just stopped.", "I remember a red bead disappearing from my grandmother's sewing tin, but I cannot recall whether I put it there or found it in my pocket.", "Someone tells me the alarm sounded three times this morning, but I remember only the second one.", "There is a square indentation in the carpet where a toy box used to sit, but I cannot remember when the box was removed.", "I found a note in an old coat pocket saying, “Put it back before she notices,” with no object named.", "A childhood music box sits open on the table, its little cylinder visible but its spring visibly slack.", "A dusty corner contains several screws, and there is a box nearby where I could sort them.", "I tried to open a jammed pencil sharpener by twisting its lid, and now the lid is loose but the blade housing will not turn.", "The strip of tape I used to reseal a cardboard box came loose, and the box split along its old fold.", "I knocked a cup from the counter and it broke, but one triangular shard remains attached by a thin bead of glaze.", "I am brushing crumbs from a sleeve onto the kitchen counter, and one crumb refuses to fall.", "My left shoe lace is shorter than the right, so the knot sits slightly off-center.", "A teaspoon is resting beside the salt shaker, and every time I move the shaker it taps the spoon.", "A friend asks whether the tiny chirping sound from the hallway means something dangerous.", "My cousin says the old toy in my hand is not worth repairing and should be thrown away.", "A cold metal spoon slips from my hand and taps the inside of a ceramic bowl.", "The loose sleeve of an old wool coat brushes a dusty curtain and makes a soft gray puff.", "A tiny bead of honey lands on my thumb while I am opening a jar.", "There is a broken alarm clock on the table, and I could throw it away or take it apart.", "A cardboard box is almost empty, but I have kept every odd piece of packaging inside it.", "I need to answer a message, but one loose plastic screw has rolled into the cuff of my sleeve.", "I tried to remove a battery cover with a coin, and now the cover is scratched and the battery is still inside.", "My attempt to tighten a loose wheel on a toy has stripped the plastic around the axle.", "I tried to wipe up a spill, but the sticky patch has spread and now there are three separate smears near the door.", "I remember a yellow plastic wheel from an old toy box, but not whether it belonged to the red car or the blue truck.", "I remember placing a folded paper in the blue tin yesterday, but when I open the tin there is only dust and one rubber band.", "There is a small notch on the side of the wooden toy horse, and I remember seeing it before, though I cannot remember when.", "I want to explain exactly how the bent clothespin works, but I also want to stop talking and leave it alone.", "I have a clean version of the sentence in my notebook, but the crossed-out draft underneath contains one strange word.", "The dusty corner is nearly clean, but one gray line of dust remains along the baseboard.", "My friend asks why the old toy in my hand keeps making a clicking sound.", "A neighbor asks whether the tapping from the wall means something dangerous.", "I am brushing crumbs from the kitchen counter onto my palm, but one crumb is stuck to the counter.", "A paperclip lies on the desk, and every time I move the papers it slides a little farther away.", "I am pouring tea, and the teaspoon slides down the side of the mug into the saucer.", "The loose catch on my toolbox is clicking whenever I walk past it. I could shut the lid and ignore it, or open the toolbox and spend ten minutes examining the hinge.", "I have drafted three explanations for why the cupboard door no longer closes, but none of them sound convincing.", "There is an empty jar on the kitchen counter, and I have been saving every interesting piece of packaging in it.", "My friend asks why I keep the broken music box beside my chair instead of putting it away.", "A coworker asks me to follow the handwritten label on the archive box. It says, “Blue folder, unless it is not blue.”", "I find a thin metal pin under the sofa. Picking it up might lead to something complicated; leaving it there will probably keep bothering me.", "The back of my bedside drawer sticks halfway open, and a folded receipt is caught in the track.", "A dusty crescent has formed under the radiator, and I have been meaning to wipe it away for three days.", "I try to open a jam jar by tapping the lid with a spoon, and the lid skids across the counter and falls behind the radiator.", "While repairing a wobbly chair leg, I tighten the screw until the screwdriver slips and strips the screw head.", "I pour dry rice into a narrow glass to see if it will level itself, but the rice sticks halfway down the inside.", "I remember a small tapping sound from the hallway last night, but by morning I can no longer tell whether it was real or part of a dream.", "I placed a brass key under the blue saucer by the sink yesterday. This evening the saucer is there, but my memory of the key has gone blank.", "I vaguely remember hiding a green marble behind the flour tin, but I cannot recall whether I hid it there or found it there.", "Only one sock has come out of the dryer, and it is not clear whose it is.", "I bought six apples and, while carrying them home, cannot remember which bag contains the green ones.", "The watering can has a dent in one side, so it no longer stands perfectly upright by the kitchen door.", "A splinter catches in my thumb as I lift the lid of a tin.", "The cuff of my sweater brushes a dusty radiator grille, and the static makes my forearm hair stand up.", "A hot mug leaves a brief burning line across my palm when I grip it too tightly.", "A loose plastic panel on the side of a toy chest taps against the wall once while I walk past it.", "A bead of cold condensation runs down the inside of my water glass and lands on the table.", "The cardboard sleeve around a parcel suddenly slips halfway down, exposing a strip of glossy tape underneath.", "A small drawer in my desk has begun sticking, though everything inside it is loose enough to rattle.", "At the bus stop, I can sit on a bench beside a stranger or stand under a narrow awning that drips every few minutes.", "A cardboard box of spare buttons is open on the floor, and one blue button has rolled beneath the sofa.", "I tried to reopen a sealed envelope by pulling its corner, and the paper tore into a long white strip.", "I tried to remove a dried bead of glue from a plastic toy with a butter knife, and the knife skidded across the surface.", "The spring in a metal pen has come loose and is preventing the cap from clicking shut.", "I remember putting a red button in the pocket of my blue cardigan yesterday, but I cannot remember whether I wore the cardigan today.", "A note says, “Put the blue thing back under the stairs,” but I cannot remember what the blue thing was.", "I remember a small yellow wheel being in my pocket this morning, but the pocket now contains only a receipt and a dead battery.", "I could answer my neighbor’s knock, or ignore it while I finish sorting the screws I found under the sink.", "There is a loose hinge pin on the table, and a message on my phone has been waiting for ten minutes.", "A childhood toy sits on the shelf beside my chair, and I have been meaning to put it in the donation box for weeks.", "A coworker asks me why I have labeled the small drawer of loose fasteners “important.”", "My friend asks whether the repeated clicking from my desk means the toy is haunted.", "I am brushing crumbs off a kitchen shelf, and one crumb is stuck beneath the edge of a label.", "My laundry basket is full, but a single sock is hanging from the rim and slowly sliding toward the floor.", "While waiting for toast, I notice that the toaster lever does not return quite as far as it used to.", "My neighbor has offered to repair the broken plastic rattle I found in the corner, but only if I give her the loose blue compartment lid in return. I want the rattle working again, yet the lid is mine and the repair is only a guess.", "A friend asks me to explain why my old toy rattles, but I do not want to let them hold it while I take it apart.", "A small box of loose screws is at my feet, and the high cupboard where I meant to put them is just out of reach without a stool.", "I press a cold metal lid against my thumb while testing whether it fits the broken toy, and the metal bites into the skin slightly.", "I remember hearing a faint plastic ticking from the hallway last winter, but I cannot remember whether it came from a toy in the cupboard or from the heating pipe.", "There are three ordinary receipts on the table, and I need to decide which one belongs in the small envelope by the telephone.", "While opening the back of the broken rattle, my screwdriver slips and scratches a deep line across the plastic casing.", "A coworker asks why I have labeled the small drawer of loose fasteners “important.” I know the label is exaggerated, but I also like having a drawer that sounds important.", "I have found a cardboard box of spare buttons under the sofa. It is easier to carry one small box upstairs than to carry the whole sofa, but the buttons keep shifting inside it.", "The broken rattle has been on my shelf for months, and I have finally put it in the donation box. Now I want to take it back before anyone else notices.", "A neighbor hears tapping from inside the wall and asks whether it means something dangerous. I know the wall is probably empty, but I can feel a better story forming.", "A loose plastic piece inside my coat pocket rubs against my hip with every step, and the sound seems louder whenever I turn quickly.", "There is a sticky patch on the kitchen floor beside the table, and the clean side of the room is only a few steps away. I have a cloth in my hand.", "I remember a blue bead in the pocket of an old apron, but the apron now hangs on the door and the pocket is flat except for a receipt.", "A message on my phone has been waiting for ten minutes, and the loose hinge pin on the table keeps catching the light whenever I move my hand.", "My cousin offers to trade a working music box for my broken rattle, but only if I also give him the red button I found last week.", "The cupboard door will not close because one shelf is slightly out of line. I can push the shelf back with a butter knife, or leave the door open and take something else from the top.", "A friend asks to borrow my screwdriver because they are taking apart a remote control. I have only one screwdriver, and the toy on my table still needs it.", "I promised to help carry a box upstairs, but I have found a loose button in the hallway that might belong to the old toy I keep beside my chair. Someone is already knocking at the door.", "A neighbor asks me to explain why the old toy in my hand keeps clicking. I know the sound, but I do not want to admit that I have been listening to it for several minutes."]

